style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.3 has been released. =
Thanks go to everyone who contributed to it!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.1.7 has come cleanly =
through QA and is pending TSC approval for =
release.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The YP TSC has now served for =
two years, thanks go to the outgoing TSC (Armin, Denys, Khem, Richard, =
Ross) who have been instrumental in a number of significant project =
developments over that time such as the LTS, definition of processes and =
resourcing the project. Some of the work isn&#8217;t immediately obvious =
but has shaped the project and should ensure a stable and positive =
future direction.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>New TSC members are now being =
chosen for the next two years. Three of the TSC seats have now been =
(re-)elected by the YP members and those seats are being filled by =
Richard (chair), Khem and Ross. Two are elected by the OE community and =
there will be a call for candidates coming soon from the OE board to the =
OE membership.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The master branch has opened =
for 3.4 development and a number of patches queued during release of 3.3 =
have now merged.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There may be interest in a new =
command, &#8220;bitbake-getvar&#8221; being proposed on the bitbake =
mailing list and in master-next. This makes it easier to see the history =
of a single variable and also makes a neat example of using the tinfoil =
API. We are also considering other similar helper commands (maybe along =
the lines of the &#8216;bb&#8217; tool) with a view to making things =
easier for new users.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent autobuilder issues =
continue to occur and are now at a record high level. You&nbsp; can see =
the list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
style=3D'mso-margin-top-alt:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin=
-left:.5in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>We are working to =
identify the load pattern on the infrastructure that seems to trigger =
these.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p =
style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs identified as =
possible for newcomers to the project: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers</spa=
n></a><o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs that are =
currently unassigned for YP 3.3. See: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Medium.2B_3.3_Unass=
igned_Enhancements.2FBugs"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Med=
ium.2B_3.3_Unassigned_Enhancements.2FBugs</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></l=
i><li style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We&#8217;d welcome new =
maintainers for recipes in OE-Core. Please see the list at: <a =
href=3D"http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/meta/conf/distro/i=
nclude/maintainers.inc"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/me=
ta/conf/distro/include/maintainers.inc</span></a> and discuss with the =
existing maintainer, or ask on the OE-Core mailing list. We will likely =
move a chunk of these to &#8220;Unassigned&#8221; soon to help =
facilitate this.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
